1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:02,127
<i>Hurry!</i>

2
00:00:02,210 --> 00:00:03,086
<i>Why--</i>

3
00:00:05,296 --> 00:00:07,173
<i>Did you think we forgot?</i>

4
00:00:07,257 --> 00:00:08,633
[OLIVER CLAPPING]

5
00:00:08,717 --> 00:00:10,468
<i>Happy birthday.</i>

6
00:00:14,556 --> 00:00:15,890
<i>Happy Birthday, Dad.</i>

7
00:00:15,974 --> 00:00:18,059
[OLIVER] <i>Make a wish! Make a wish!</i>

8
00:00:18,727 --> 00:00:19,644
[OLIVER] <i>Boom!</i>

9
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:23,022
[CHUCKLES]

10
00:00:23,106 --> 00:00:25,859
[ENRICO]<i> I wished that</i>
<i>we'd always be like this.</i>

11
00:00:27,235 --> 00:00:28,278
<i>Happy</i>

12
00:00:29,946 --> 00:00:31,656
<i>and all together.</i>

13
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:34,075
[OLIVER] <i>Of course, Papa.</i>

14
00:00:34,159 --> 00:00:35,952
<i>We won't be apart anymore.</i>

15
00:00:36,911 --> 00:00:38,204
<i>Right, Billy?</i>

16
00:00:39,497 --> 00:00:40,582
<i>Yes, that's right.</i>

17
00:00:42,917 --> 00:00:44,419
<i>We're finally complete.</i>

18
00:00:50,216 --> 00:00:52,719
[PRECIOUS] <i>Enrico, are you really okay?</i>

19
00:00:52,802 --> 00:00:54,471
<i>Billy and I noticed earlier</i>

20
00:00:54,554 --> 00:00:56,681
<i>that you seemed to have something</i>
<i>weighing on your mind.</i>

21
00:00:56,765 --> 00:00:57,891
<i>Is something bothering you?</i>

22
00:00:58,808 --> 00:01:02,937
<i>I requested that, if possible,</i>
<i>she be transferred to a hospital.</i>

23
00:01:03,021 --> 00:01:05,690
<i>We're already monitoring her condition.</i>

24
00:01:05,774 --> 00:01:06,900
<i>That's not enough!</i>

25
00:01:06,983 --> 00:01:09,944
<i>Is my request that hard?!</i>
<i>My mother needs--</i>

26
00:01:10,487 --> 00:01:14,074
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

27
00:01:24,083 --> 00:01:25,293
<i>I was wrong, Ma.</i>

28
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:28,463
<i>The truth won't hurt us.</i>

29
00:01:30,632 --> 00:01:32,801
<i>It may even save us both.</i>

30
00:01:36,805 --> 00:01:38,139
[PRECIOUS] <i>Of course.</i>

31
00:01:39,057 --> 00:01:41,351
<i>Bea would do anything for her mother.</i>

32
00:01:41,434 --> 00:01:43,645
<i>Just like you would for your father.</i>

33
00:01:44,354 --> 00:01:47,607
<i>What happened to us was devastating.</i>

34
00:01:48,733 --> 00:01:50,652
<i>But when I found out</i>

35
00:01:52,028 --> 00:01:54,697
<i>that Dad didn't forget about me,</i>

36
00:01:55,907 --> 00:02:00,829
<i>everything we had lost</i>
<i>didn't seem to matter anymore.</i>

37
00:02:02,413 --> 00:02:05,125
<i>Because Dad came back to us.</i>

38
00:02:07,085 --> 00:02:09,587
[ENRICO]<i> Have you found</i>
<i>my wife and daughters?</i>

39
00:02:09,671 --> 00:02:12,382
<i>I'm afraid I have some bad news.</i>

40
00:02:13,424 --> 00:02:16,636
<i>Your eldest daughter, Abigail?</i>

41
00:02:20,890 --> 00:02:22,809
<i>She died in a fire.</i>

42
00:02:22,892 --> 00:02:29,357
FIRE BURNS DOWN HOME

43
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:30,775
[ENRICO] <i>Abi, dear…</i>

44
00:02:32,527 --> 00:02:34,237
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

45
00:02:35,113 --> 00:02:37,949
<i>I wasn't a good father to you and Bea.</i>

46
00:02:40,702 --> 00:02:42,036
<i>I promise…</i>

47
00:02:44,205 --> 00:02:46,583
<i>I will find your mother and sister.</i>

48
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:49,377
<i>I don't know if Billy will ever</i>
<i>be able to forgive me</i>

49
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:51,421
<i>for what I'm about to tell her.</i>

50
00:02:51,504 --> 00:02:53,131
<i>I know this is too much.</i>

51
00:02:53,798 --> 00:02:55,884
<i>But she needs to know the truth.</i>

52
00:02:57,093 --> 00:02:58,094
Attorney.

53
00:02:59,095 --> 00:03:02,098
I can request to speak to Billy, right?

54
00:03:03,683 --> 00:03:06,686
I can just relay your message to her.

55
00:03:07,812 --> 00:03:08,730
No.

56
00:03:08,813 --> 00:03:12,233
I have to tell her myself.
We need to talk in person.

57
00:03:13,234 --> 00:03:16,863
Well, we can make a request.

58
00:03:17,488 --> 00:03:19,908
But there's no guarantee
that she'll agree.

59
00:03:20,658 --> 00:03:23,453
And besides, I'm your lawyer.

60
00:03:24,203 --> 00:03:27,790
Anything you intend to say to her
should go through me first.

61
00:03:28,791 --> 00:03:32,378
I know that.
But this is a personal matter.

62
00:03:32,462 --> 00:03:36,883
So I want to talk to her alone
and tell her myself.

63
00:03:37,967 --> 00:03:39,594
Whatever it is,

64
00:03:40,303 --> 00:03:42,263
it's better if I know.

65
00:03:42,972 --> 00:03:45,350
Because it might aggravate your case

66
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:47,936
even if you have good intentions.

67
00:03:49,812 --> 00:03:51,940
What is it that you want
to say to Ms. Cariño?

68
00:03:52,023 --> 00:03:56,361
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

69
00:03:56,444 --> 00:03:57,403
Attorney.

70
00:03:58,571 --> 00:03:59,989
Please submit a request

71
00:04:00,073 --> 00:04:03,076
so I can personally talk to Billy.

72
00:04:03,159 --> 00:04:10,083
[STIRRING MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

73
00:04:15,922 --> 00:04:22,637
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

74
00:04:59,882 --> 00:05:02,385
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

75
00:05:06,097 --> 00:05:10,268
[GLUM MUSIC PLAYING]

76
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:27,452
Okay.

77
00:05:28,453 --> 00:05:29,662
Moving forward,

78
00:05:30,872 --> 00:05:32,957
we need to find a new investor.

79
00:05:35,418 --> 00:05:37,378
We've already put
a lot of money into this.

80
00:05:37,462 --> 00:05:39,172
We can't let this fall through.

81
00:05:40,548 --> 00:05:41,591
Uh…

82
00:05:41,674 --> 00:05:42,508
Chief?

83
00:05:42,592 --> 00:05:49,015
What about our tie-up
with the mega-influencers in the US?

84
00:05:49,098 --> 00:05:52,810
They're set to release
their content next week.

85
00:05:53,478 --> 00:05:54,812
And

86
00:05:54,896 --> 00:05:57,190
we've already paid them a down payment.

87
00:05:57,982 --> 00:05:59,108
Down payment?

88
00:05:59,192 --> 00:06:00,610
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

89
00:06:00,693 --> 00:06:02,862
I didn't sign anything like that.

90
00:06:03,446 --> 00:06:04,405
[MARJ] Uh…

91
00:06:04,489 --> 00:06:06,157
Y-You see, chief,

92
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:08,659
we thought it was a done deal.

93
00:06:08,743 --> 00:06:13,498
And you said we needed to act fast.

94
00:06:13,581 --> 00:06:16,167
Even so. It still should have
gone through me.

95
00:06:16,918 --> 00:06:18,002
Toni.

96
00:06:18,086 --> 00:06:20,004
You released the budget for that?

97
00:06:20,088 --> 00:06:22,256
- I also thought--
- You also thought?!

98
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:24,967
Can we please stop working
based on assumptions?!

99
00:06:25,051 --> 00:06:27,678
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

100
00:06:27,762 --> 00:06:29,305
Like I said,

101
00:06:29,931 --> 00:06:32,058
this project needs to push through.

102
00:06:32,141 --> 00:06:35,353
We've already issued a press release.
People are expecting!

103
00:06:35,937 --> 00:06:38,314
Marj. Put that on hold.

104
00:06:40,817 --> 00:06:44,070
We need to find potential investors.

105
00:06:44,153 --> 00:06:45,571
If not Claire, then who?

106
00:06:45,655 --> 00:06:47,073
If not the US, then where?!

107
00:06:48,116 --> 00:06:49,951
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

108
00:06:50,034 --> 00:06:51,536
Um…

109
00:06:51,619 --> 00:06:56,332
Ralph and I can plan an investors' gala.

110
00:06:56,415 --> 00:06:58,251
We can tap into his network.

111
00:06:59,377 --> 00:07:02,880
There is an upcoming Asian investor summit

112
00:07:02,964 --> 00:07:04,590
that will be held in Cebu.

113
00:07:05,133 --> 00:07:07,093
I can secure tickets for us.

114
00:07:07,176 --> 00:07:09,804
Val,
work with Marj.

115
00:07:09,887 --> 00:07:14,100
Since there will surely be a delay,
keep our market engaged.

116
00:07:14,183 --> 00:07:16,811
Call whoever needs to be called.

117
00:07:16,894 --> 00:07:17,979
Will do.

118
00:07:22,567 --> 00:07:29,574
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

119
00:07:47,008 --> 00:07:48,176
Enrico.

120
00:07:48,968 --> 00:07:52,263
Enrico, you're starting to worry me.
Is your blood sugar still low?

121
00:07:52,805 --> 00:07:53,723
Wait right here.

122
00:07:54,307 --> 00:07:55,224
Precious.

123
00:07:55,308 --> 00:07:59,353
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

124
00:07:59,437 --> 00:08:01,105
I have something

125
00:08:02,064 --> 00:08:03,357
to tell you and Billy.

126
00:08:05,234 --> 00:08:06,986
I just don't know how to say it

127
00:08:07,069 --> 00:08:09,614
because I don't want to hurt you again.

128
00:08:09,697 --> 00:08:11,240
Especially Billy.

129
00:08:12,492 --> 00:08:13,618
What is it?

130
00:08:14,911 --> 00:08:17,413
You know what happened to me in Canada.

131
00:08:17,497 --> 00:08:19,999
But there's still something
I haven't told you.

132
00:08:21,459 --> 00:08:23,002
After I got released,

133
00:08:24,587 --> 00:08:27,215
as well as looking for Billy…

134
00:08:29,383 --> 00:08:30,968
I also looked for…

135
00:08:33,012 --> 00:08:34,764
my other family.

136
00:08:34,847 --> 00:08:41,395
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

137
00:08:41,479 --> 00:08:43,523
Have you inquired with the contractors?

138
00:08:44,106 --> 00:08:45,066
Yes, chief.

139
00:08:45,149 --> 00:08:48,736
Since the fire did major damage
to your house,

140
00:08:48,819 --> 00:08:53,032
they said it will cost
around 2.5 to 3 million.

141
00:08:53,616 --> 00:08:55,368
That's a huge amount.

142
00:08:56,202 --> 00:08:59,413
Have you made a deposit
into my account this month?

143
00:09:00,039 --> 00:09:01,207
But, chief,

144
00:09:02,333 --> 00:09:04,043
this has also arrived.

145
00:09:05,878 --> 00:09:09,757
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

146
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:12,802
Monthly statement of your second mortgage.

147
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:21,561
Okay.

148
00:09:23,062 --> 00:09:24,689
- [BLAIRE] Okay.
- Thank you.

149
00:09:28,442 --> 00:09:30,444
Strong coffee for a strong woman.

150
00:09:34,031 --> 00:09:35,658
I don't think this is enough.

151
00:09:35,741 --> 00:09:38,077
We're going to stay up all night at work.

152
00:09:39,287 --> 00:09:40,246
Thank you.

153
00:09:42,665 --> 00:09:48,296
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

154
00:09:48,379 --> 00:09:49,380
[VALERIE] Jordan?

155
00:09:50,131 --> 00:09:51,882
Jordan! Oh my God!

156
00:09:51,966 --> 00:09:53,843
Our video went viral!

157
00:09:53,926 --> 00:09:56,637
Three hundred thousand views!
Look, look, look! Look!

158
00:09:56,721 --> 00:09:59,432
That's great.
But, Val, that can wait.

159
00:09:59,515 --> 00:10:01,017
Huh? Why?

160
00:10:01,809 --> 00:10:05,229
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

161
00:10:05,313 --> 00:10:06,397
Oh my God.

162
00:10:06,981 --> 00:10:09,400
Oh my gosh, Billy, I'm so sorry.

163
00:10:09,483 --> 00:10:10,610
[BILLY] It's fine.

164
00:10:10,693 --> 00:10:16,532
I just got so excited because
I uploaded a video of him singing, and…

165
00:10:17,199 --> 00:10:18,743
I don't know.

166
00:10:18,826 --> 00:10:21,203
That evening, when he was singing,

167
00:10:21,287 --> 00:10:23,039
there was just something in him.

168
00:10:23,122 --> 00:10:25,166
With the way he sang the song.

169
00:10:25,249 --> 00:10:27,084
How do I put this? Um…

170
00:10:27,752 --> 00:10:29,795
Heartfelt? Special?

171
00:10:29,879 --> 00:10:31,297
And then that was it.

172
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:32,840
After I uploaded it,

173
00:10:32,923 --> 00:10:35,301
the video went viral.

174
00:10:35,384 --> 00:10:36,427
- [SQUEALS]
- Okay.

175
00:10:36,510 --> 00:10:37,678
Let's talk about it later.

176
00:10:37,762 --> 00:10:39,347
Come on. Let's go.

177
00:10:39,430 --> 00:10:40,556
Give her some space.

178
00:10:41,599 --> 00:10:42,516
[JORDAN] Sorry.

179
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:49,565
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

180
00:10:55,363 --> 00:10:58,741
[JORDAN SINGING IN VIDEO]
<i>♪ My muse ♪</i>

181
00:10:58,824 --> 00:11:02,745
<i>♪ Where's our destination? ♪</i>

182
00:11:03,996 --> 00:11:06,957
<i>♪ You are the captain ♪</i>

183
00:11:07,041 --> 00:11:10,836
<i>♪ I'll follow wherever you go ♪</i>

184
00:11:11,671 --> 00:11:13,005
<i>♪ Oh, baby ♪</i>

185
00:11:13,089 --> 00:11:17,385
<i>♪ I'll ride your wave ♪</i>

186
00:11:17,468 --> 00:11:21,555
<i>♪ Wherever it takes me ♪</i>

187
00:11:21,639 --> 00:11:24,350
<i>♪ Do you know when I found you ♪</i>

188
00:11:24,433 --> 00:11:26,394
<i>♪ Everything changed? ♪</i>

189
00:11:27,228 --> 00:11:30,022
<i>♪ Wherever I go ♪</i>

190
00:11:30,106 --> 00:11:34,276
<i>♪ My heart won't be lost ♪</i>

191
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:38,572
<i>♪ Even if you let go, I'll come back ♪</i>

192
00:11:38,656 --> 00:11:41,492
<i>♪ Do you know when I found you ♪</i>

193
00:11:41,575 --> 00:11:43,577
<i>♪ Everything changed? ♪</i>

194
00:11:44,286 --> 00:11:46,705
<i>♪ Wherever I go ♪</i>

195
00:11:46,789 --> 00:11:49,500
<i>♪ I'm coming home ♪</i>

196
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:53,879
I feel like such a failure.

197
00:11:53,963 --> 00:11:56,257
I disappointed our chief again.

198
00:11:56,882 --> 00:12:00,636
I thought I was doing a good job,
or at least, a decent job.

199
00:12:01,971 --> 00:12:05,015
Hey, don't take it to heart.
It's just work.

200
00:12:05,099 --> 00:12:06,392
Mm-hmm.

201
00:12:06,475 --> 00:12:08,602
Don't take it to heart?

202
00:12:08,686 --> 00:12:11,230
You're one to talk.

203
00:12:11,313 --> 00:12:13,732
I saw how negative
your vibe became earlier.

204
00:12:14,608 --> 00:12:19,738
Guys, let's just focus on
our deliverables first, okay?

205
00:12:19,822 --> 00:12:21,073
Let's not fixate on that,

206
00:12:24,827 --> 00:12:28,164
- Psst. Hey. Morrie, focus.
- [JORDAN SINGING ON SPEAKER]

207
00:12:28,247 --> 00:12:31,584
<i>♪ It seems I'm drowning in sorrow ♪</i>

208
00:12:32,168 --> 00:12:33,502
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

209
00:12:33,586 --> 00:12:34,962
Well…

210
00:12:35,045 --> 00:12:39,091
I was the one who uploaded
Jordan's performance video.

211
00:12:40,384 --> 00:12:42,178
Wrong timing, Val.

212
00:12:43,888 --> 00:12:45,890
You know we have
a lot of problems right now.

213
00:12:50,811 --> 00:12:52,980
I shouldn't have raised my voice earlier.

214
00:12:53,063 --> 00:12:56,650
[JORDAN SINGING ON SPEAKER]
<i>♪ I'll follow wherever you go ♪</i>

215
00:12:57,359 --> 00:12:59,695
[PHONE VIDEO MUSIC STOPS,
SOMBER MUSIC PLAYS]

216
00:12:59,778 --> 00:13:00,779
Marj…

217
00:13:03,324 --> 00:13:04,241
Toni…

218
00:13:05,534 --> 00:13:06,410
I'm sorry.

219
00:13:06,494 --> 00:13:09,663
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

220
00:13:10,247 --> 00:13:14,710
And dude, congratulations
on your viral performance.

221
00:13:17,379 --> 00:13:18,589
It's nothing.

222
00:13:18,672 --> 00:13:19,673
No big deal.

223
00:13:20,508 --> 00:13:21,842
No big deal?

224
00:13:23,093 --> 00:13:24,345
Hello?

225
00:13:24,428 --> 00:13:26,722
I know. Can we just…

226
00:13:28,057 --> 00:13:29,850
No. Val is right.

227
00:13:29,934 --> 00:13:31,185
It is a big deal.

228
00:13:31,268 --> 00:13:34,605
More people should see your talent.

229
00:13:34,688 --> 00:13:35,814
And you know,

230
00:13:35,898 --> 00:13:39,026
I know why your performance went viral.

231
00:13:41,237 --> 00:13:43,322
I mean, I can really feel your emotions.

232
00:13:44,782 --> 00:13:45,658
Congrats.

233
00:13:51,247 --> 00:13:52,665
[PHONE RINGING]

234
00:13:53,832 --> 00:13:56,418
[CLEARS THROAT]
Excuse me, I'll just take this.

235
00:13:57,378 --> 00:13:58,754
Hello, Billy?

236
00:13:58,837 --> 00:14:00,339
Hello, Attorney?

237
00:14:00,422 --> 00:14:03,592
I just got off the phone
with Atty. Reyes, Bea's lawyer.

238
00:14:03,676 --> 00:14:06,470
Bea asked to speak with you in person.

239
00:14:06,554 --> 00:14:07,638
Why?

240
00:14:08,138 --> 00:14:09,515
She wouldn't say.

241
00:14:09,598 --> 00:14:13,644
Can't she just say whatever it is
through her lawyer?

242
00:14:14,144 --> 00:14:15,813
[SIGHS] Bea's adamant.

243
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:18,357
She insists it's a… family matter?

244
00:14:19,567 --> 00:14:20,568
Okay.

245
00:14:21,402 --> 00:14:23,404
I'll pay her a visit. Thank you.

246
00:14:23,988 --> 00:14:30,244
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

247
00:14:33,122 --> 00:14:35,666
- [MUSIC FADES]
- [BIRDS CHIRPING]

248
00:14:35,749 --> 00:14:37,376
[VALERIE] Going back to our topic…

249
00:14:37,459 --> 00:14:38,669
[INHALES SHARPLY]

250
00:14:38,752 --> 00:14:41,380
The reason why your video went viral

251
00:14:41,463 --> 00:14:44,925
was because your energy
is just so genuine.

252
00:14:45,009 --> 00:14:47,469
Like, it's so natural.

253
00:14:47,553 --> 00:14:50,848
And your performance was super sincere.

254
00:14:50,931 --> 00:14:52,016
It was like…

255
00:14:53,309 --> 00:14:55,519
You could really feel that
you were in love--

256
00:14:55,603 --> 00:14:56,478
Val!

257
00:14:57,187 --> 00:14:58,480
Can we talk?

258
00:14:59,815 --> 00:15:00,774
Over here.

259
00:15:00,858 --> 00:15:05,905
["THE PUZZLE"
BY BELLE MARIANO PLAYING]

260
00:15:08,741 --> 00:15:09,992
Stop it.

261
00:15:10,576 --> 00:15:12,077
Why? I'm just stating facts.

262
00:15:13,370 --> 00:15:16,665
As you sang, it was like
you poured everything out.

263
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:21,003
Everyone felt it because you were
being honest, Jordan.

264
00:15:21,670 --> 00:15:24,673
Except for that one person
you dedicated that song to.

265
00:15:26,008 --> 00:15:27,509
The person you love.

266
00:15:31,513 --> 00:15:38,520
["THE PUZZLE" CONTINUES]

267
00:15:41,523 --> 00:15:43,567
HOUSE RAZED BY FIRE
ELDEST DAUGHTER DEAD, MOTHER HURT

268
00:15:43,651 --> 00:15:45,277
[ENRICO] I want to apologize to them too.

269
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:51,533
They're your family?

270
00:15:51,617 --> 00:15:53,661
[SOFT, DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

271
00:15:53,744 --> 00:15:56,080
Bea Mercado is your daughter?

272
00:15:56,872 --> 00:15:59,541
Are you married to Mariela Mercado?

273
00:16:00,542 --> 00:16:02,002
You know them?

274
00:16:02,086 --> 00:16:05,381
Mercado is Mariela's maiden name.

275
00:16:05,464 --> 00:16:07,591
How do you know them?

276
00:16:07,675 --> 00:16:11,470
Enrico, it wasn't an accident
when our house caught fire.

277
00:16:12,471 --> 00:16:14,306
It was Mariela's doing.

278
00:16:15,808 --> 00:16:17,309
How is that possible?

279
00:16:18,644 --> 00:16:20,562
They're in jail.

280
00:16:21,605 --> 00:16:24,108
Both Mariela and Bea, your daughter.

281
00:16:24,191 --> 00:16:26,944
She hid her mother from the police.

282
00:16:27,027 --> 00:16:30,030
But that's not at all, Enrico.
There's more.

283
00:16:30,114 --> 00:16:33,534
Billy has filed many more cases
against them.

284
00:16:33,617 --> 00:16:35,911
They wouldn't leave her alone.

285
00:16:35,995 --> 00:16:38,038
They wanted to ruin her life.

286
00:16:38,122 --> 00:16:41,458
Your wife and your daughter.

287
00:16:41,542 --> 00:16:43,585
So that's why they're so mad at us.

288
00:16:44,795 --> 00:16:47,881
That's why Mariela called me a mistress.

289
00:16:47,965 --> 00:16:49,550
<i>I saw my husband.</i>

290
00:16:50,509 --> 00:16:52,720
<i>The one who hasn't contacted me in years.</i>

291
00:16:54,847 --> 00:16:55,973
<i>I caught him</i>

292
00:16:56,932 --> 00:16:58,559
<i>with another woman again.</i>

293
00:16:59,268 --> 00:17:00,936
<i>He has a new mistress.</i>

294
00:17:01,645 --> 00:17:03,272
[SIGHS] <i>Mariela…</i>

295
00:17:03,355 --> 00:17:05,065
<i>She took him away from me!</i>

296
00:17:05,691 --> 00:17:07,860
<i>I wanted to kill them!</i>

297
00:17:07,943 --> 00:17:10,154
[DRAMATIC MUSIC BUILDS]

298
00:17:10,237 --> 00:17:12,406
<i>If it wouldn't have meant</i>
<i>leaving my daughter behind,</i>

299
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:15,284
<i>if it wouldn't have landed me in prison,</i>

300
00:17:15,367 --> 00:17:17,661
<i>I would've killed them!</i>

301
00:17:17,745 --> 00:17:21,290
<i>My husband and his lover!</i>

302
00:17:22,124 --> 00:17:24,752
<i>Mariela, what you're thinking is wrong.</i>
<i>You can't do that.</i>

303
00:17:24,835 --> 00:17:29,006
And that's why Bea claims that
Billy stole something from her.

304
00:17:29,089 --> 00:17:31,925
Because they believe
we stole you from them!

305
00:17:32,593 --> 00:17:34,595
That Billy stole you from them!

306
00:17:37,014 --> 00:17:38,682
I'd like to see them.

307
00:17:38,766 --> 00:17:45,564
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

308
00:17:45,647 --> 00:17:47,691
[MUSIC FADES]

309
00:17:49,818 --> 00:17:52,613
[PHONE VIBRATING]

310
00:17:52,696 --> 00:17:58,619
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

311
00:18:13,801 --> 00:18:15,427
Mister, please hurry up.

312
00:18:22,017 --> 00:18:28,899
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

313
00:18:37,032 --> 00:18:39,076
[MUSIC FADES]

314
00:18:46,875 --> 00:18:48,293
You wanted to speak with me.

315
00:18:50,129 --> 00:18:52,923
I don't have all day.
I'm a busy person.

316
00:18:54,967 --> 00:18:56,468
Billy, sorry.

317
00:18:57,219 --> 00:19:00,931
Have you run out of tricks
to escape from this?

318
00:19:01,014 --> 00:19:05,185
Your apology won't erase
all the harm you've done to my family.

319
00:19:06,103 --> 00:19:08,397
I trusted you, Bea. Remember?

320
00:19:09,189 --> 00:19:10,816
I tried to understand you.

321
00:19:10,899 --> 00:19:13,610
I asked you countless times
for your motive,

322
00:19:13,694 --> 00:19:15,445
but I never got an answer.

323
00:19:16,196 --> 00:19:19,491
You just kept making things worse
for my family.

324
00:19:20,242 --> 00:19:21,243
[EXHALES HEAVILY]

325
00:19:21,326 --> 00:19:25,038
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

326
00:19:25,122 --> 00:19:26,498
Billy, you're right.

327
00:19:27,457 --> 00:19:29,042
I wronged you.

328
00:19:29,126 --> 00:19:31,003
I wronged your family too.

329
00:19:35,174 --> 00:19:36,592
I did it because you stole from me.

330
00:19:36,675 --> 00:19:39,011
Bullshit! I never stole anything from you.

331
00:19:39,595 --> 00:19:41,471
You tore my family apart, Billy,

332
00:19:41,555 --> 00:19:44,224
Because you stole my father from us.

333
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:51,815
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

334
00:20:00,741 --> 00:20:01,950
<i>Look at this.</i>

335
00:20:02,034 --> 00:20:04,494
- [JORDAN SINGING IN VIDEO]
<i>- That's my daughter's song!</i>

336
00:20:04,578 --> 00:20:05,579
<i>Jade wrote that!</i>

337
00:20:05,662 --> 00:20:07,331
<i>That's right, Grandpa!</i>

338
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:08,707
<i>- Yes.</i>
- [CHUCKLING]

339
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:14,046
[JORDAN] <i>That song is for</i>
<i>the two women I love the most.</i>

340
00:20:14,129 --> 00:20:15,547
<i>Watch it, man.</i>

341
00:20:15,631 --> 00:20:17,341
- [WHISTLE BLOWS]
- [CRASHES]

342
00:20:17,424 --> 00:20:19,051
- [INMATE 1] <i>Hey!</i>
- [INMATE 2] <i>You bastard!</i>

343
00:20:19,134 --> 00:20:20,135
[PRISONERS CLAMORING]

344
00:20:20,219 --> 00:20:21,845
[BILLY] <i>I never stole</i>
<i>anything from you.</i>

345
00:20:22,429 --> 00:20:24,306
<i>You tore my family apart, Billy.</i>

346
00:20:24,389 --> 00:20:27,059
<i>Because you stole my father from us.</i>

347
00:20:28,435 --> 00:20:29,436
<i>Billy?</i>

348
00:20:33,941 --> 00:20:35,067
<i>Bea?</i>

349
00:20:35,150 --> 00:20:36,443
<i>Sweetheart?</i>

350
00:20:41,156 --> 00:20:43,367
<i>I'm asking again</i>
<i>for forgiveness, dear.</i>

351
00:20:43,450 --> 00:20:44,910
<i>From both of you.</i>

352
00:20:44,993 --> 00:20:47,329
<i>You're seriously asking</i>
<i>for forgiveness?</i>

353
00:20:47,412 --> 00:20:49,414
<i>My sister died.</i>
<i>Your daughter died!</i>

354
00:20:49,498 --> 00:20:53,001
<i>She was your daughter!</i>
<i>Your eldest daughter!</i>

355
00:20:53,085 --> 00:20:55,879
<i>- I'll make it up to you.</i>
<i>- You can't change anything now!</i>

356
00:20:55,963 --> 00:20:57,631
<i>Dad? Dad!</i>

357
00:20:57,714 --> 00:20:59,675
[GROANING IN PAIN]

358
00:21:00,592 --> 00:21:01,760
[BEA] <i>Help!</i>
